# Client data must never reach the repository. This tool is pointed at real
# exports -- contact records with names, emails, phone numbers and birth
# dates -- and the GitHub remote is public. An accidental `git add -A` is
# the only thing standing between a demo file and a disclosure.
#
# Anything dropped in the working directory to be assessed is data, not
# source. Keep it that way.
*.csv
*.tsv
*.xlsx
*.xls
*.json.gz

# Run artifacts: data/runs/{id}/source.csv is a verbatim copy of whatever
# was uploaded, so this directory is as sensitive as the uploads themselves.
data/
*.sqlite
*.db

# Generated reports carry the data they describe.
*.pdf
!dqa-architecture-v1.png

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
.env
.env.local

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/

# Working notes from the frontend team, kept locally rather than in the repo.
BACKEND_CHANGES.md
